    body: "The 1st ZRR Visit of the Rotaract Club of Metro City on November 29, 2025, served as a comprehensive review and documentation of the club’s efforts, activities, and progress for the current Rotaract year. Conducted at the Moliss College, the visit included formal presentations from each avenue director, showcasing the club’s completed projects, ongoing initiatives, and future plans through structured reports, documentation, and visual presentations.\n\nThe session highlighted key accomplishments across community service, professional development, international service, club administration, finance, and public relations, reflecting the club’s dedication to impactful service and organizational growth. Directors also presented their records, meeting minutes, and project evidence as required by the ZRR checklist, ensuring transparency and alignment with district standards. An interactive discussion followed, where members received guidance, identified areas for improvement, and explored opportunities for collaboration at the zonal and district levels. This visit not only strengthened internal accountability but also reaffirmed the club’s commitment to excellence, collaboration, and continuous improvement within Rotaract District 3292.",
