    excerpt: "The session was fruitful and informative. Also, it helped our club in international exposure.",
    body: "With the aim of spreading the awareness to empower teenagers to understand themselves better, break social taboos, and build healthier, more confident lives, we Rotaract Club of Metro City collaborated with the Rotaract Club of Social Crew of RID 3250 and organized a session on Physical Health and Personal Hygiene under the Project Unfiltered led by Dr. Dikshya Acharya.\n\nThe session covered key areas such as mental health and emotional well-being, confidence, consent and communication, and the importance of seeking help. It also included open conversations on body changes during adolescence menstruation, mood swings, and physical development for girls, and voice cracks, facial hair, and societal pressures for boys reinforcing that these changes are completely normal.\n\nWith the aim of empowering teenagers, the project encouraged participants to understand themselves better, break social taboos, and build healthier, more confident lives.",
