    body: "OXSA Nepal is an animal shelter dedicated to the rescue, care, and protection of animals-mainly dogs, cats, and birds. Currently, the shelter houses 22 dogs, 1 cat, and 1 crow, providing them with food, shelter, and necessary healthcare services.\n\nOn 24th August 2025, Rotaract Club of Metro City , jointly with its twin club Rotaract Club of Metrocity, successfully organised an OXSA Donation Programme .Members from both clubs actively participated, showcasing unity, service spirit, and shared commitment to animal welfare.As a gesture of support and compassion, RAC Durbarmarg and RAC Metrocity jointly donated:\n\n2 packs of rice (25 kg each)\n\n5 kg of lentils\n\n2 crates of eggs\n\nThe total cost of these items was equally shared between both clubs. This contribution helped fulfil the nutritional needs of the animals and supported the shelter in managing its daily operations.\n\nDuring the visit, members from both clubs interacted with the caretaker of OXSA Nepal. They learned about:\n\nThe day-to-day challenges of running an animal shelter\n\nThe health and nutritional needs of the animals\n\nThe importance of continuous community involvement and donations\n\nThis meaningful exchange deepened members’ understanding and compassion towards animal welfare.",
    objectives: "The initiative aimed to:\n\nSupport the welfare of animals under OXSA’s care\n\nPromote awareness about animal rights and animal-related humanitarian service\n\nEncourage members to participate in service projects beyond human-centric causes\n\nStrengthen bonds between twin clubs through meaningful collaboration",
