    gallery: ["https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1764298313-3478697b-8ebc-46c7-be30-4d46f4e29a84.jpg", "https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1764298313-8f6fe909-2a97-4162-8dce-244f40346bfb.jpg"],
    excerpt: "Conducting an installation ceremony helps formally transition leadership and recognize incoming board members. It also strengthens club unity, renews commitment, and showcases the…",
    body: "The 14th Installation Ceremony of the Rotaract Club of Metro City was a dignified and well-organized event held to officially transfer leadership responsibilities and celebrate the achievements of the club. The program commenced with the arrival and acknowledgment of distinguished guests, including club leaders, district officials, and respected invitees. Following the National and Rotary anthems, the lighting of the Panas symbolized the formal inauguration of the ceremony. A warm welcome address and a graceful cultural performance added vibrance and warmth to the occasion.\n\nOutgoing President Rtr. Sweta Shrestha delivered a comprehensive annual report outlining the club’s initiatives and achievements over the past year. Certificates of appreciation were then awarded to board members and contributors in recognition of their dedication and service. The incoming President Rtr. Anusha Pandey was formally introduced, took her oath of office, and was presented with the club’s insignia - including the charter certificate, collar, gong, and gavel - representing the official transfer of leadership. In her acceptance speech, she shared her vision for the coming year and announced the newly appointed board members, who also took their oaths and received badges and identification cards.\n\nThe ceremony further featured the induction of new members, remarks from dignitaries, and special acknowledgments honoring the contributions of the outgoing president. Tokens of appreciation were distributed to guests and supporters as a gesture of gratitude. Ending on a gracious note, a vote of thanks was delivered, followed by a formal toast for national and international harmony and goodwill. The event concluded with the adjournment by the newly installed president and informal fellowship over refreshments.\n\nThe ceremony exemplified the club’s commitment to leadership development, continuity of service, and a strengthened spirit of Rotaract camaraderie.",
    objectives: "To officially induct new president, board of directors and members, marking the formal beginning of the new tenure (RY 2025-26).",
