    excerpt: "The COTS helped members clearly understand their roles, responsibilities, and improved leadership, teamwork, and overall club involvement.",
    body: "Here’s a simplified and Metro City-based version in the same style:\n\nOn 19th July 2025, members of the Rotaract Club of Metro City actively participated in the Zonal Club Officers Training Seminar (COTS) held at Mid Valley International College, Kathmandu. The program was organized to help Rotaract members from different clubs within the zone better understand their roles and responsibilities in their respective clubs.\n\nThe training included position-based sessions where participants were divided into separate groups according to their roles. This allowed members to have focused discussions and clearly understand what is expected from their specific positions.\n\nThe interactive nature of the seminar encouraged active participation, making the learning experience both informative and engaging. Members were able to share ideas, learn from others, and build connections with fellow Rotaractors from different clubs. The session helped strengthen their sense of responsibility, teamwork, and commitment toward club activities.\n\nOverall, the event was a meaningful experience that not only provided useful knowledge but also helped build friendships and motivation among participants. It inspired members to contribute more actively and effectively in their Rotaract journey ahead.",
    objectives: "To help members understand their roles and responsibilities within their respective club positions. To provide position-based training for better clarity of duties and expectations. To improve leadership skills and strengthen organizational understanding among Rotaract members. To encourage teamwork, communication, and active participation within the club. To create awareness about effective club functioning and available opportunities in Rotaract",
