    excerpt: "The 18th DLTS provided participants with enhanced leadership capabilities, improved communication and team collaboration skills, and valuable district-level networking opportunities…",
    body: "The 18th District Leadership Training Seminar (DLTS), organized by the Rotaract Club of Patan Heritage, was a premier leadership development initiative focused on strengthening leadership, communication, and collaboration skills among Rotaractors. Held at the Nepal Police Club, the event featured a rich schedule of expert-led sessions, team-building activities, and fellowship opportunities, all designed to empower and connect club leaders from across the district.\n\nRotaract Club of Metrocity was honored to collaborate in this impactful event. Our members actively supported coordination efforts and participated enthusiastically in all training and fellowship sessions.\n\nThe event was especially rewarding for our club, as we were recognized for our achievements and contributions throughout the tenure:\n\n🏆 Holique - Awarded as Best Public Image Chair Project\n\n🏅 Yomari Fest - Recognized as a Signature Club Administration Event\n\n🥈 Vibrant Silver Recognition - For overall energetic and consistent club performance\n\n📜 Club Recognition Certificate - Awarded to RAC Metrocity for exceptional dedication and impact\n\n🌟 Rtr. DRR Aid Utsav Shrestha, a proud member of our club, received a special recognition from the District Rotaract Representative (DRR) for his commitment and contribution to the district\n\nThis event not only served as a learning platform but also celebrated fellowship, teamwork, and the collective spirit of service that drives the Rotaract movement.",
