    excerpt: "The one-time meal distribution and donation at Anmol Bal Griha provided immediate nutritional support to 21 children, enhancing their well-being. The gaming equipment donation…",
    body: "Rotaract Club of Metrocity conducted a heartwarming one-time meal distribution and donation program at Anmol Bal Griha, located at Kathmandu Metropolitan City -31, Kharibot, Kathmandu. The initiative aimed to bring smiles and comfort to the 21 children (comprising 16 boys and 5 girls) residing there, aged between 4-5 to 15-16 years.\n\nThis event, planned as a regular community service activity, coincidentally coincided with the birthday of our member, Rtr. Nirogya Prasain, making the day even more memorable. Along with the meal, the club also donated gaming equipment to support the children’s recreational and mental well-being.\n\nThe project was further enhanced by the active involvement of one proposed member, promoting engagement and inclusivity within the club.\n\nThe combination of thoughtful service, joyful interaction, and heartfelt giving made this initiative a truly meaningful experience-upholding the Rotaract values of fellowship, service, and community impact.",
    objectives: "To provide a nutritious one-time meal to the children of Anmol Bal Griha.\n\nTo donate gaming equipment and support recreational activities for the children.\n\nTo engage club members, including a proposed member, in meaningful community service.\n\nTo foster a culture of compassion by coinciding service with personal milestones.\n\nTo strengthen the club’s connection with local orphanages and promote long-term goodwill.",
