    body: "On 23rd May 2025, the Rotaract Club of Metro City hosted its 380th General Meeting via Google Meet, with the primary agenda being the official visit of the Zonal Rotaract Representative (ZRR) Rtr. Diya Shrestha of Zone XII. The meeting commenced at 9:00 PM and was attended by 12 club members, including the club president, board members, and general members. The session began with a warm welcome by Club Secretary Rtr. Anusha Pandey, followed by the opening of the meeting by Club Admin Rtr. Uday Lamichhane and President Rtr. Sweta Shrestha.\n\nPresident Rtr. Sweta Shrestha formally welcomed ZRR Rtr. Diya Shrestha, acknowledging her presence as a great encouragement to the club. The ZRR then took the floor, introducing herself and elaborating on her roles, responsibilities, and the broader objectives of the zonal structure. She emphasized the importance of active communication, timely reporting, and collaboration among clubs in the zone. Her presence created a platform for mutual learning and exchange.\n\nThe visit was marked by a comprehensive project presentation session. Club Secretary Rtr. Anusha Pandey presented a slide deck highlighting the club’s recently completed projects, outlining the objectives, outcomes, and social impact of each initiative. Following this, the avenue directors provided individual updates from their respective service domains, showcasing the club’s engagement across all five avenues. The ZRR responded with encouraging remarks, appreciating the club’s well-documented efforts, diverse projects, and balanced focus on both professional and community service. She particularly commended the club’s attention to detail and project reporting, suggesting continued momentum and increased participation in zonal and district events.\n\nThe visit served as an important milestone in the club’s annual calendar, reinforcing its alignment with zonal goals and enhancing motivation among members. The interaction with the ZRR was both insightful and reassuring, strengthening the club’s commitment to service and growth. The meeting concluded with discussions around the upcoming DRR visit, scheduled for 24th May 2025, and was officially adjourned at 10:15 PM.",
    objectives: "To officially host and engage with ZRR Rtr. Diya Shrestha, strengthening the club’s connection with zonal leadership.To present the club’s key projects and accomplishments for review, ensuring transparency and alignment with zonal goals.To gather constructive feedback and guidance from the ZRR to improve club performance and member engagement.",
