    excerpt: "The MOU signing between RAC Metro City and its twin club RAC Durbarmarg marked a significant step toward deeper collaboration, enabling both clubs to pool their strengths for greater…",
    body: "On the occasion of its Charter Day, the Rotaract Club of Metro City signed a Memorandum of Understanding (MOU) with its Twin Club, the Rotaract Club of Durbarmarg, on 17th May at Aura Rooftop Restaurant, Gaushala, Kathmandu. This significant event marked a reaffirmation of fellowship, collaboration, and shared vision between the two clubs.\n\nThe MOU symbolizes a commitment to mutual support, joint project implementation, leadership development, and ongoing exchange of ideas and resources. Both clubs pledged to promote stronger inter-club relations by participating in each other’s events and working together toward impactful community service.\n\nThe signing took place in the gracious presence of District Committee Members, including District Rotaract Representative (DRR)-Aide Rtr. Utsav Shrestha and Assistant District Leadership Trainer (ADLT) Rtr. Ruchin Khadka, who congratulated both clubs and encouraged meaningful collaboration.\n\nThe ceremony, conducted as part of the Charter Day celebration, was marked by enthusiasm, camaraderie, and the spirit of unity, making it a memorable milestone in the journey of both clubs.",
    objectives: "To strengthen the bond of friendship and collaboration between RAC Metro City and its twin club, RAC Durbarmarg.To formalize mutual commitment toward shared goals and joint initiatives.To encourage regular participation in each other’s events and activities.To promote the exchange of ideas, experiences, and best practices for club growth.To foster leadership development and teamwork through inter-club cooperation.To increase the impact of community service by leveraging combined resources and efforts.To uphold the values of Rotaract through sustained partnerships and unity.",
