    excerpt: "The Charter Day Celebration of RAC Metro City served as a powerful reminder of the club’s legacy and impact. It strengthened member bonds, renewed their commitment to service, and…",
    body: "On 17th May 2025, the Rotaract Club of Metro City joyfully celebrated its Charter Day, marking the 12th anniversary since the club's inception. This event was held to honor the journey of the club-from its humble beginnings to becoming a vibrant platform for service, leadership, and personal development.\n\nThe celebration was a reflective and joyous occasion. A short video presentation showcased the club’s key milestones, impactful service projects, achievements, and cherished memories over the past 12 years. Past Presidents and senior members shared their experiences and extended their good wishes, creating a nostalgic and inspiring atmosphere.\n\nThe program also featured fun games, cake-cutting, and an informal fellowship session that allowed members to bond and celebrate the legacy they are building together. Members expressed their gratitude to everyone who contributed to the club’s growth and reaffirmed their commitment to carrying the torch forward.\n\nThe event boosted morale, reignited the sense of belonging and pride among members, and provided a perfect opportunity to reflect on past achievements while planning for an even more meaningful future. It served as a motivating platform to continue working together in the true spirit of Rotaract.\n\nThe Charter Day celebration was a memorable success. With enthusiastic participation, heartfelt speeches, and meaningful moments, the event truly honored the legacy and spirit of Rotaract Club of Metro City.",
    objectives: "To commemorate the founding of the Rotaract Club of Metro City and honor its journey since charter.To boost morale and reignite a sense of pride and belonging among club members.To reflect on the club’s past achievements and milestones.To strengthen fellowship and unity within the club through shared celebration.To inspire and motivate members for greater participation in future initiatives.To reinforce the values and vision of Rotaract among new and existing members.To foster a deeper commitment towards continued service and leadership.",
