    gallery: ["https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1747940574-224d8bda-ea54-4ef2-8681-d6688d342e32.jpeg", "https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1747940574-ea91f9a6-7e8a-42af-a07b-0bcb677c5e91.jpeg", "https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1747940574-5055a683-654f-4eae-a500-ff55b5cf5349.jpeg", "https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1747940574-f369df33-b85f-4862-82b7-9544fd72dbaf.jpeg", "https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1747940574-39017d0d-584f-43f8-aaa5-7e13a3891faf.jpeg", "https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1747940574-96422061-f41a-4b84-82bd-d6572605844e.jpeg"],
    excerpt: "The Mandala Therapy Workshop 2.0 provided participants with a creative and calming space to explore mindfulness, emotional expression, and self-healing through art. It enhanced…",
    body: "The Rotaract Club of Metro City had the privilege of co-hosting the impactful and creatively healing session titled “Mandala Therapy 2.0”, organized by the Rotaract Club of Kathmandu Metro. This unique wellness and art-focused workshop was designed to help participants explore mindfulness, self-awareness, and emotional balance through the creation of mandalas.\n\nThe session was led by the inspiring Rtr. Aakriti Bharati, who brought her expertise and passion to the room as the facilitator. She guided attendees through the spiritual and cultural heritage of mandalas, elaborating on their symbolism in Eastern traditions such as Hinduism and Buddhism, where they represent wholeness, balance, and the cosmos.\n\nParticipants learned how these sacred designs have also been embraced in modern therapeutic practices, particularly through Carl Jung’s psychological interpretations of mandalas as tools for self-reflection and inner healing. The workshop also delved into color theory, showing how colors influence emotions and how their use in mandala art can be therapeutic.\n\nThe interactive session empowered attendees to engage in hands-on mandala creation using materials provided as part of the registration. This immersive experience allowed them to disconnect from external stressors, focus on the present moment, and embrace the meditative rhythm of creativity.\n\nAs a co-hosting partner, the Rotaract Club of Metro City proudly contributed to the seamless execution of the event, promotion, and overall vibrancy of the session. The collaboration reflected the power of collective effort within the Rotaract movement to prioritize mental wellness and holistic growth.",
    objectives: "Promote Mental Wellness: To create a safe and reflective space for participants to prioritize their mental and emotional health through a guided therapeutic activity. Introduce Mandala Art as Therapy: To familiarize participants with the history, spiritual significance, and psychological benefits of mandala art in both Eastern traditions and modern therapeutic contexts.Enhance Self-Awareness and Mindfulness: To encourage participants to engage in mindful creativity, helping them cultivate greater self-awareness, focus, and inner balance.Educate on Color Theory and Emotions: To provide insight into basic color theory and how the strategic use of colors can influence emotions, mood, and psychological healing.Encourage Artistic Expression: To inspire individuals to use art as a medium of self-expression and emotional release, regardless of artistic background or skill level.Foster Community Engagement: To strengthen collaboration among Rotaract Clubs and build a supportive community dedicated to wellness, creativity, and service.",
