    excerpt: "The event enhanced leadership skills, deepened inter-club connections, and strengthened team spirit. RAC Metro City members gained valuable insights, built meaningful networks, and…",
    body: "The Rotaract Club of Metro City, as one of the proud co-hosts, actively contributed to the grand success of the 2nd Presidents and Secretaries Meet (PS Meet) and Presidents-Elect and Secretaries-Elect Training Seminar (PETS/SETS) held at Galaxy Garden Resort, Chitwan. The event, a key fixture in the Rotaract District 3292 calendar, brought together Rotaractors from across the country for a full day of learning, leadership, and fellowship.\n\nRAC Metro City showcased a strong presence with enthusiastic participation from its members, who played vital roles in event management, coordination, and member engagement throughout the program. From supporting logistics and registration to facilitating hospitality and smooth session flow, the club remained actively involved in every aspect of the event. Our members not only ensured a welcoming atmosphere for attendees but also reinforced our commitment to collaboration and service through their seamless teamwork and proactive involvement.\n\nThe training sessions offered during the program were both informative and inspiring, equipping incoming leaders with essential tools and insights for the upcoming Rotaract term. Members of RAC Metro City attentively participated in the sessions and contributed to meaningful discussions, reflecting the club's dedication to continuous learning and leadership development.\n\nFollowing the formal sessions, the post-event fellowship brought another dimension to the day. With vibrant dance performances and cultural exchanges, the evening allowed members to unwind, celebrate, and strengthen connections across clubs. This informal gathering fostered unity and created lasting memories, especially as it provided the opportunity to interact with Rotaractors from all corners of the country.\n\nRAC Metro City's involvement in this flagship event once again highlighted our commitment to strengthening the Rotaract movement through active participation, leadership development, and collaborative spirit. The club's contribution to the success of the 2nd PS Meet and PETS/SETS was recognized and appreciated by the organizing committee and fellow Rotaractors, reinforcing our reputation as a reliable and energetic presence in District 3292.",
    objectives: "To support and co-host a flagship district training event with active participation.To equip incoming club leaders with knowledge, skills, and strategies for effective leadership.To foster collaboration, networking, and fellowship among Rotaractors from across the country.To strengthen the club's presence and commitment within District 3292 through proactive involvement.",
