    id: "50659",
    title: "Session on LinkedIn Optimization",
    slug: "session-on-linkedin-optimization-50659",
    avenue: "International Service",
    projectType: "Collaborated",
    tenure: "2024-25",
    status: "Completed",
    date: "2025-03-23",
    location: "Google Meet",
    category: "Training / Workshops",
    cover: "https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1747935166-9b95de6b-7435-41a1-8ce2-37b57156677c.jpg",
    gallery: ["https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1747935166-9b95de6b-7435-41a1-8ce2-37b57156677c.jpg"],
    excerpt: "The session empowered participants with practical LinkedIn strategies to enhance their professional presence and global networking skills.",
    body: "The “LinkedIn Optimization Session” was held virtually on 23rd March 2025 (10th Falgun, 2081 BS) via Google Meet, organized by the RAC JIMS Vasant Kunj jointly with Rotaract Club of Metro City. The session featured Mr. Varunn Joshi a LinkedIn Expert, as the guest speaker. As an experienced professional with a strong LinkedIn presence, Mr. Joshi guided participants through the process of building a compelling and impactful LinkedIn profile.\n\nThe session was highly interactive, with active participation from attendees throughout. Mr. Joshi shared detailed, actionable strategies for profile enhancement, including optimizing headlines, writing a professional ‘About’ section, leveraging keywords, and strategically growing one’s network. He also revealed lesser-known features and techniques to boost visibility and credibility on the platform-valuable insights that are often overlooked.\n\nParticipants were encouraged to ask questions, and the Q&A segment helped clarify common doubts about job-seeking, content creation, and engagement on LinkedIn. The session was informative, engaging, and practical, allowing members to immediately apply what they learned.\n\nOverall, it was a fruitful and enriching session that not only improved digital professionalism among members but also stood out as a successful international collaborative project. The partnership between RAC Metro City and RAC JIMS Vasant Kunj helped bridge ideas across borders and made this initiative a proud international-level success for the club.",
    objectives: "· To equip members with the tools to create a professional LinkedIn profile.\n\n· To enhance members’ online presence for career and networking opportunities.\n\n· To provide practical tips for optimizing LinkedIn profiles and content strategy.\n\n· To foster collaboration and knowledge-sharing among clubs.\n\n· To successfully execute an international-level professional development project, expanding the club's reach and recognition.",
