    cover: "https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1747836931-d2ef8e9d-9e88-4647-a198-02fe1237f0ac.jpg",
    gallery: ["https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1747836931-d2ef8e9d-9e88-4647-a198-02fe1237f0ac.jpg", "https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1747836931-4a0129cc-1e8d-4bea-81ed-6e86617e9def.jpg"],
    excerpt: "The Nationwide Cleaning Campaign enhances environmental sustainability, fosters community responsibility, and raises awareness about cleanliness and proper waste disposal.",
    body: "The Nationwide Cleaning Campaign, a flagship initiative organized by Rotaract District 3292, was actively and successfully conducted by the Rotaract Club of Lalitpur on 22nd March 2025 at Bagmati Corridor (Sankha Park), Lalitpur. The campaign witnessed enthusiastic participation from the Rotaract Club of Metro City along with all the clubs under Zone XII, creating a powerful impact through collective action and shared responsibility. The campaign was primarily focused on promoting environmental sustainability, addressing urban waste issues, and fostering civic responsibility among youth and the community. With gloves, masks, and cleaning tools in hand, Rotaractors-joined by members of the local police-dedicated their efforts to cleaning the riverbanks, collecting waste, and raising awareness about the significance of maintaining clean public spaces. Volunteers worked diligently to remove litter from the Bagmati Corridor, not only enhancing the physical environment but also setting an example of proactive citizenship. Beyond the physical cleanup, the campaign served as a platform to engage the public in important conversations about waste management and the long-term importance of environmental protection. The visibility and commitment shown by Rotaractors during the event reflected the spirit of service and environmental stewardship that lies at the heart of the Rotaract movement. Overall, the Nationwide Cleaning Campaign at Sankha Park was a resounding success. It not only beautified a vital section of the Bagmati River but also inspired community members to take ownership of their surroundings and adopt sustainable habits. The Rotaract Club of Metro City is proud to have been part of this impactful initiative and remains committed to supporting future actions that promote a cleaner, greener Nepal.",
    objectives: "To promote environmental sustainability and awareness among Rotaractors and the general public.To address urban waste issues by cleaning and managing litter in public spaces.To encourage community participation and responsibility in maintaining cleanliness.To foster collaboration among Rotaract clubs under District 3292 and Zone XII.To set an example of proactive civic engagement and environmental stewardship.To support long-term behavioral change regarding proper waste disposal and hygiene practices.To enhance the aesthetic and ecological value of the Bagmati Corridor (Sankha Park).",
