    id: "50231",
    title: "Yomari Fest 2025",
    slug: "yomari-fest-2025-50231",
    avenue: "Club Administration",
    projectType: "Hosted",
    tenure: "2024-25",
    status: "Completed",
    date: "2025-02-22",
    location: "Shrey Courtyard,Tinkune, Kathmandu",
    category: "Signature Project",
    cover: "https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1747650981-757f07b9-fd19-4a28-b733-00ec5e923505.jpeg",
    gallery: ["https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1747650981-757f07b9-fd19-4a28-b733-00ec5e923505.jpeg", "https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1747650981-3facfdd6-a3d4-48b7-8a2a-8ea37cb691c6.jpeg", "https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1747650981-2372a5a3-3126-409c-b50e-1e10ff163539.jpeg", "https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1747650981-7d6fbd25-ab40-4f06-be08-96e2fde5f6ec.jpg", "https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1747650981-bfb6f70d-576d-4094-a2ee-32f8567ec66e.jpg", "https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1747650981-7adc4137-f2d4-4f1e-9f5f-3a0996ad511e.jpg"],
    excerpt: "It enhanced the club’s visibility and reputation by showcasing its ability to organize a large-scale cultural and charitable event, attracting wide community participation and media…",
    body: "Yomari Fest 2025, the flagship cultural and charitable event organized by the Rotaract Club of Metro City, was held on February 22, 2025, at the scenic Shrey Courtyard in Kathmandu. Hosted in collaboration with co-host clubs-the Rotaract Club of Bhadgaon and the Rotaract Club of Central Valley Kasthamandap-the event was a vibrant celebration of Newari heritage, traditional cuisine, and community service. From the outset, the event created an immersive atmosphere, drawing in a large and enthusiastic crowd of Rotaractors, cultural enthusiasts, and the general public. Traditional performances such as the iconic Lakhey dance, the graceful Kumari dance, and the resonant beats of the Dhimey Baja captivated the audience. Many attendees embraced the festive spirit by wearing traditional Newari attire, including Hakupatasi and Daura Suruwal, which added to the authenticity and richness of the celebration.\n\nA major highlight of the festival was its culinary showcase, with the beloved Yomari-a steamed dumpling filled with chaku and khuwa-symbolizing prosperity and festivity, served alongside a variety of other Newari delicacies. The authentic flavors delighted attendees and deepened their appreciation for Newari food traditions. The event also featured live music, interactive games, and fun-filled activities like Bingo, keeping the crowd fully engaged. The atmosphere was electric with joy, laughter, and excitement, and by all measures, the event was a huge success. Participants and guests expressed overwhelming satisfaction and happiness, making it clear that the event exceeded expectations.\n\nMore than just a cultural fest, Yomari Fest 2025 carried a powerful social message. All proceeds from the event were dedicated to supporting the students of Shree Prajajyoti Secondary School in Chepang Basti, with the goal of promoting educational opportunities for underprivileged children. This charitable element underscored the event’s dual mission of preserving culture while contributing to community welfare. Rtr. Sweta Shrestha, President of the Rotaract Club of Metro City, highlighted that the event not only celebrated tradition but also aimed to make a meaningful difference in society. Co-host club presidents, Rtr. Binayak Dahal of RAC Bhadgaon and Rtr. Aayush Pokhrel of RAC Central Valley Kasthamandap, expressed their delight at the event’s success and the unity it fostered among clubs and communities. Yomari Fest 2025 was a perfect fusion of culture, entertainment, and compassion, leaving participants with lasting memories, deeper cultural appreciation, and the joy of having supported a noble cause.",
    objectives: "• To celebrate and promote the vibrant culture and traditions of the Newar community.\n\n• To showcase traditional Newari music, dance, attire, and cuisine.\n\n• To create a platform for cultural exchange and community bonding.\n\n• To raise funds to support the education of students from Shree Prajajyoti Secondary School, Chepang Basti.\n\n• To foster collaboration among Rotaract Clubs and strengthen inter-club relationships.\n\n• To blend cultural celebration with meaningful community service and social impact.",
    metrics: [{ label: "Attendees", value: "246" }, { label: "Volunteer hrs", value: "364" }, { label: "Budget", value: "NRs 58,475" }, { label: "Members", value: "16" }],
    partners: ["RAC Bhadgaon", "Rac Central Valley Kasthamandap"],
    goals: ["To open and develop collaboration and connectedness", "To establish Club's Public image", "Networking and Fellowship", "Service in community"],
    coordinators: ["Rtr. Utsav Shrestha", "Rtr. Sweta Shrestha", "Rtr. Uday Lamichhane"],
