    tenure: "2024-25",
    status: "Completed",
    date: "2025-02-19",
    location: "Indradevi Madhyamic Vidhalaya",
    category: "RNLM (TEACH)",
    cover: "https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1747672572-c807ff19-b734-4c31-b481-7dd07e49726f.jpeg",
    gallery: ["https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1747672572-c807ff19-b734-4c31-b481-7dd07e49726f.jpeg", "https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1747672572-cd2d02e2-c72e-4f71-9ab2-fba9747388c3.jpeg", "https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1747672572-7e302291-e617-4071-a836-945dfb8d6d9a.jpeg", "https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1747672572-85e680b5-94fe-413e-b57e-be32a2bf11f0.jpeg"],
    excerpt: "Helps them in continuing education, reduces burden on families, promote sense of community and support, Increased community involvement, Increased networking with other organizations",
    body: "We successfully collaborated the project \"Sapna Sikshya Abhiyan\" at Indradevi Madhyamic Vidhalaya, Kavre Panauti-12, in the collaboration with Leo club of Kathmandu Chabahil and Rotaract Club of Gyaneswor CIST on Feb 19. Through this initiative, we provided stationary items, educational session about Astronomical devices, and shared knowledge about their significance.\n\nPre-Event phase: In the wake of recent devastating floods in many regions, many family suffered severe losses due to which affected their ability to support their children's education. Realizing the urgent need to step in and help. With a goal of supporting underprivileged students by providing them with essential stationary items, a detailed survey was conducted to identify students who were most affected by the flood and unable to afford basic learning materials.\n\nAfter seeing the impactful program, we saw interest in it. As a supporting club, we donated funds.\n\nConclusion : Project Sapna Sikshya Abhiyan successfully fulfilled its goal of supporting students in need during a critical time. It not only provided them with essential supplies but also renewed hope and spirit of learning among young minds. The event was carried out in an organized and respectful manner, maintaining the dignity of every child. Smiles and gratitude filled the room as the students received the stationary items. The initiative helped restore a sense of motivation in the students. The school has decided to continue similar outreach programs in the future and explore long-term educational support for affected children.",
    objectives: "To support children in continuing their education without interruption by providing essential learning materialsTo ease the financial stress on families affected by the flood who cannot afford to buy school suppliesTo promote equal learning opportunities for all children",
