    gallery: ["https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1748183560-ef2688ee-b0ba-484f-9a8a-3f9abc4ceee3.jpg"],
    excerpt: "The session equipped members with practical project management skills, boosting their confidence to plan and execute impactful and well-structured club initiatives.",
    body: "On 18th January 2025, after the 371st General Meeting, the Rotaract Club of Metro City successfully conducted a Speaker Session on Project Management via Google Meet. The session featured Rtr. Ruchin Khadka, a dedicated Rotaractor and a certified Assistant District Leadership Trainer (ADLT), who brought his expertise in project planning and execution to the virtual platform. The objective of the session was to equip club members with practical tools and knowledge for managing club and community projects more effectively.\n\nDuring the session, Rtr. Khadka covered key aspects of project management, including goal setting, stakeholder analysis, budgeting, timeline planning, risk management, and post-project evaluation. He emphasized the importance of clarity in objectives, team coordination, and documentation for successful project delivery. The session was interactive, with members asking questions about real-life project challenges and sharing their own experiences.\n\nThis knowledge-sharing session was highly beneficial in strengthening members’ capacity to plan and lead impactful projects. It not only enriched their organizational skills but also helped align club efforts with structured project management practices. Overall, the session proved to be both insightful and motivating, especially for young Rotaractors looking to take on leadership roles in service and professional development.",
    objectives: "To enhance members’ understanding of the fundamental principles of project management.To provide practical tools and techniques for effective planning, execution, and evaluation of projects.To build members’ confidence in leading and managing club and community initiatives.To promote structured, goal-oriented, and sustainable project practices within the club.",
