    gallery: ["https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1747937602-87113c1c-3259-4721-8154-9cc1aa2981dd.jpeg", "https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1747937602-89e36955-fb72-4b1f-a034-3887c9427ad7.jpeg", "https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1747937602-349c57f9-613c-4444-9dd9-3f126a49c15a.jpeg", "https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1747937602-80e1f782-602d-4fde-89fc-99163cefeb6b.jpeg", "https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1747937602-dcfe3bb1-2704-46e3-b3fb-8963c35d501c.jpeg"],
    excerpt: "Participation in the 17th District Conference proved highly beneficial for the Rotaract Club of Metro City. It offered our members a dynamic platform to network with Rotaractors from…",
    body: "The Rotaract Club of Metro City proudly participated in the 17th Rotaract District Conference, held on the 3rd and 4th of January 2025 at the BICC in Butwal. Organized by Rotaract District 3292 and graciously hosted by the Rotaract Club of Butwal South, this landmark event brought together Rotaractors from across Nepal, creating a vibrant space for dialogue, collaboration, and celebration.\n\nOur club members were actively engaged in the conference, participating in insightful panel discussions, interactive sessions, and leadership-focused workshops. These sessions emphasized Rotaract values, community service, and strategies for sustainable change, aligning closely with our club’s vision for impact. A defining moment of the event was the District Rotaract Representative (DRR) election, in which our club president Rtr. Sweta Shrestha had the honor of casting the official vote on behalf of the club. Rtr. Prakash Sharma was elected as the next DRR, signaling a new phase of leadership for the district.\n\nBeyond formal proceedings, the event offered a powerful platform for networking. With the presence of representatives from over 180 Rotaract clubs, our members were able to build valuable relationships, explore collaboration opportunities, and share experiences that enriched our collective purpose. Cultural programs and dance performances added color and warmth to the event, reinforcing fellowship and unity within the Rotaract movement.\n\nThe conference also served as a moment of pride, as a few of our members were acknowledged for their commitment and considered for upcoming district responsibilities. The exposure, connections, and leadership insights gained through this conference are set to inspire our club's activities in the coming term.\n\nIn essence, the 17th District Conference proved to be a memorable and transformative experience for RAC Metro City. It reaffirmed our commitment to service, fellowship, and leadership while expanding our network across the district.",
    objectives: "Promote Leadership Engagement: Take part in the DRR election process to support democratic leadership and understand the functioning of Rotaract governance.Foster Club Networking: Connect and collaborate with Rotaractors from over 180 clubs across the nation, building relationships for future joint projects and initiatives.Enhance Skills & Knowledge: Participate in thematic workshops, panel discussions, and training sessions to strengthen leadership, communication, and project management skills.Celebrate Rotaract Unity: Embrace the cultural diversity of Rotaract through performances, exhibitions, and social activities that promote fellowship and shared values.Encourage Member Representation: Provide club members a platform to be recognized and considered for district-level positions and responsibilities.Drive Community Impact: Gather ideas, inspiration, and strategies from other clubs to improve the planning and execution of impactful community service projects.",
