    date: "2024-12-14",
    location: "MOLISS College, Kumaripati, Lalitpur",
    category: "District Event",
    cover: "https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1747663664-407f18b2-21c6-4efe-96ff-f5857d6decad.jpg",
    gallery: ["https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1747663664-407f18b2-21c6-4efe-96ff-f5857d6decad.jpg", "https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1747663664-fcb46c34-612e-4c9d-8d61-577e03763105.jpg", "https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1747663664-ffa6977f-081a-45a2-80af-291029836871.jpg"],
    excerpt: "Conducting the Zonal Quiz helped in promoting fellowship and healthy competition among clubs in the zone. It enhanced members’ knowledge of Rotary, Rotaract, and general awareness…",
    body: "The Rotaract Club of Metro City successfully hosted the zonal round of the Late Rtr. Santosh Memorial Quiz for Zone XII on 14th December 2024 at MOLISS College, Kumaripati. This intellectually stimulating event brought together Rotaractors from across the zone to compete, connect, and celebrate the spirit of learning and fellowship.\n\nThe program began promptly at 11:00 AM, adhering strictly to the scheduled timeline, which reflected the event’s excellent time management and organizational discipline. The quiz was conducted in strict accordance with the official guidelines set and provided by the District Quiz Committee, ensuring transparency, fairness, and standardization across the rounds.\n\nDistrict Rotaract Representative Aide Rtr. Utsav Shrestha took charge as the Quiz Master, conducting the event with great energy and professionalism. His leadership contributed to the smooth and engaging flow of the quiz. The presence of Zonal Rotaract Representative Rtr. Diya Shrestha further added to the significance of the event, as she actively supported and encouraged the participants.\n\nA key highlight of the program was the interactive component, where questions left unanswered by the competing teams were passed to the audience. This segment energized the room and encouraged enthusiastic participation from everyone present. Prizes were awarded for correct answers, making the audience feel equally involved.\n\nRefreshments were served to all participants, Rotaractors, and audience members, adding to the warm hospitality and overall positive experience. The event served not only as a competitive platform but also as an opportunity for learning, networking, and strengthening bonds within the Rotaract community.\n\nIn summary, the zonal round of the Late Rtr. Santosh Memorial Quiz was a well-executed, punctual, and lively event that upheld the values of Rotaract through knowledge, collaboration, and camaraderie.",
    objectives: "The objective of the Zonal Quiz in Rotaract is to enhance members' knowledge of Rotaract, Rotary, and current affairs while promoting fellowship, teamwork, and healthy competition among clubs within the zone.\n\n• To honor the memory and contributions of Late Rtr. Santosh through a meaningful and educational event.\n\n• To foster a spirit of healthy competition and intellectual growth among Rotaractors of Zone XII.\n\n• To encourage teamwork, quick thinking, and knowledge-sharing within and across Rotaract clubs.\n\n• To provide a platform for Rotaractors to engage with Rotary and Rotaract values through learning.\n\n• To promote fellowship and inter-club interaction through a fun and interactive quiz environment.\n\n• To identify and prepare competent teams for the district-level round of the quiz.\n\n• To build confidence, public speaking, and stage presence among participating members.\n\n• To enhance overall engagement by including audience participation and reward-based learning.",
