    excerpt: "The 11th Late Rtr. Sachin Memorial Blood Donation Program not only helped save lives through the collection of vital blood units but also reinforced the values of service and…",
    body: "The 11th Late Rtr. Sachin Memorial Blood Donation Program was jointly organized by the Rotaract Clubs of Zone XII in loving memory of Late Rtr. Sachin, a dedicated and compassionate Rotaractor whose legacy of service continues to inspire. The program took place with strong participation from Rotaractors and members of the local community, collecting a total of 47 units of blood to support patients in need. The event served as a tribute to Rtr. Sachin’s spirit of giving and aimed to promote the culture of voluntary blood donation.\n\nThis life-saving initiative was further strengthened by the valuable support of Lalitpur Metropolitan City, whose involvement added both institutional backing and encouragement to the event. The drive created awareness about the importance of regular blood donation, highlighted community responsibility, and engaged youth in meaningful action. More than just a service program, it was a reflection of unity, compassion, and commitment to making a difference. The event also reinforced fellowship and collaboration among the clubs of Zone XII, fostering a collective spirit of giving and remembrance.",
    objectives: "To honor and commemorate the selfless service of Late Rtr. Sachin through a meaningful and impactful initiative.To promote the importance of voluntary blood donation and raise public awareness about its life-saving potential.To collect blood units to support individuals in urgent medical need.To foster a sense of community involvement and social responsibility among Rotaractors and the general public.To strengthen unity, fellowship, and collaboration among the Rotaract Clubs of Zone XII.",
