    excerpt: "Project Benefit Note: 1. Improved Survival Rates: By providing food and blankets, the project helps flood victims meet their basic survival needs, reducing hunger. 2. Enhanced Physical…",
    body: "Project Details:\n\nThe \"Rations and Blanket Distribution to Flood Victims\" was a community service initiative organized by Rotaract Club of Metro City supported by Rotary Club of Kathmandu Metro and Bhojan Unlimited to help 25 families in Nakkhudol, Lalitpur affected by the flood in 28th September,2024. This project took place when we first distributed cooked meals to the victims at Nakkhu. More than one time cooked meal, they were in need of rations and blankets. Thus, the project planning was done and action was taken accordingly.\n\nThis program included:\n\nDistribution of essential supplies, including food items (1 sack of rice, 3kg pulse, packet of oil, half kg soya chunks) and blanket to each family.\n\nNeed assessment done before distribution to be able to help the most affected ones.\n\nThe budget of the project included food, blankets, transportation and logistics.",
    objectives: "Project Objectives:\n\nTo Facilitate the Flood Victims with their Basic Needs such as Food and Clothes.\n\nTo distribute blankets to provide warmth and protection to those displaced by the floods, especially in harsh weather conditions.\n\nTo Collect Relief Materials and Funds for \"Rations and Blanket Distribution to Flood Victims\".\n\nTo continuously assess the evolving needs of the flood victims to adjust the type and quantity of aid provided.",
