    cover: "https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1748182969-b48184c2-8b31-4ff8-b998-18b2efaa508d.jpg",
    gallery: ["https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1748182969-b48184c2-8b31-4ff8-b998-18b2efaa508d.jpg", "https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1748182969-4aa0c856-ca79-4895-90f7-0c8e73fd7b9c.jpg"],
    excerpt: "The session broadened participants' understanding of urban poverty and slum conditions, encouraging empathy, civic responsibility, and interest in sustainable urban development and…",
    body: "On 28th September 2024, following the 365th General Meeting, the Rotaract Club of Metro City organized a thought-provoking Speaker Session on Slum Awareness at MOLISS College, Kumaripati, Lalitpur. The session was led by Er. Deepak Shrestha, a civil engineer and urban development advocate known for his work on housing and informal settlements. The aim of the session was to sensitize Rotaractors and attending students about the realities of slum life in Nepal and the social, infrastructural, and policy challenges associated with it.\n\nDuring the session, Er. Shrestha provided an in-depth overview of urban slums, focusing on their causes, rapid urban migration, lack of planning, and systemic gaps in urban governance. He also presented case studies from various slum settlements in Kathmandu Valley, highlighting issues such as poor sanitation, housing insecurity, and limited access to basic services. Emphasizing a humane and inclusive approach, Er. Shrestha urged youth to advocate for participatory urban planning and sustainable development.\n\nThe interactive nature of the session allowed participants to engage in meaningful discussions and reflect on the role of young professionals in addressing urban inequality. The session not only raised awareness but also inspired attendees to consider slum rehabilitation and urban resilience as areas for future service projects and research. Overall, the program contributed to the club’s ongoing commitment to social awareness and responsible civic engagement.",
    objectives: "To raise awareness among Rotaractors and students about the living conditions and challenges faced by slum communities in Nepal.To educate participants on the causes of slum development, urban migration, and gaps in urban planning.To encourage dialogue on sustainable solutions for slum rehabilitation and inclusive urban development.To inspire youth engagement in community development and policy advocacy related to housing and infrastructure.",
