    excerpt: "The session enhanced members’ understanding of electrical safety and protection measures, encouraging safer practices in daily life and professional settings. It also inspired future…",
    body: "On 28th September 2024, immediately following the 364th General Meeting of the Rotaract Club of Metro City, a speaker session on \"Electrical Protection Awareness\" was successfully conducted. The session featured Er. Rabindra Shrestha, Former Deputy Head of the Nepal Electricity Authority, as the keynote speaker. With decades of experience in electrical engineering and national infrastructure, Er. Shrestha provided valuable insights into electrical safety practices, protection mechanisms, and risk mitigation strategies in both household and industrial contexts.\n\nDuring the session, Er. Shrestha discussed common electrical hazards, the importance of earthing and circuit breakers, and practical tips to prevent electrical accidents. He also introduced the latest technologies and safety measures adopted by NEA and emphasized the importance of public awareness in reducing electrical mishaps. The session was highly informative and interactive, with participants actively engaging in a Q&A session that followed the presentation.\n\nThe event proved to be a highly beneficial knowledge-sharing platform, enhancing the members' technical understanding of electrical protection and safety protocols. It also inspired ideas for community-level awareness programs in the future. Overall, the session aligned with the club’s goal of promoting professional development among its members while contributing meaningfully to public safety education.",
    objectives: "Enhanced technical literacy and safety awareness among Rotaractors.Inspired club members to consider community-based awareness projects on electrical safety.Strengthened the club’s engagement in professional development and knowledge sharing.",
