    gallery: ["https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1747749952-256a24c4-a883-4bb1-8ea1-cdf1a7ea2e9d.jpeg", "https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1747749952-e31a72b2-ffbf-4dfc-9854-9788dcd2c948.jpeg", "https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1747749952-2eb99069-b708-44b6-923b-5cf14c5c93c6.jpg", "https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1747749952-60c8c288-3690-4a8f-a864-f9f4a4a01002.jpg"],
    excerpt: "The program \"Teej with Rotaractor Aayo Bari Lai\" fostered stronger fellowship among Rotaractors, enhanced inter-club coordination, and provided a joyful platform to celebrate culture…",
    body: "On the joyful occasion of Teej, a vibrant cultural fellowship event titled “Teej with Rotaractor Aayo Bari Lai” was successfully organized on Saturday, August 31st, 2024, at Tribhuwan University, Smriti Bhawan, Kirtipur. The event was a collaborative effort led by the Rotaract Club of Kantipur and the Rotaract Club of Kathmandu West, with the enthusiastic support of co-host clubs-Rotaract Club of Kathmandu Metropolis, Rotaract Club of Metro City, and Rotaract Club of Tribhuwan University.\n\nThe celebration commenced at 4:00 PM and brought together Rotaractors in a lively atmosphere filled with cultural expression and camaraderie. The program began with an engaging fellowship game, “Fire in the Mountain, Run Run Run,” hosted by Rtr. Ronit Shrestha. This was followed by an electrifying welcome dance by the host clubs, setting a high-spirited tone for the rest of the evening.\n\nThroughout the program, various co-host clubs performed dance, song, and poetry, showcasing the diverse talents within the Rotaract community. Interactive games kept the audience entertained, while food and accessories stalls attracted continuous visits, adding flavor and fun to the gathering.\n\nAn open mic session created space for spontaneous performances and self-expression, where many Rotaractors came forward to share their talents. The event concluded with a group dance session, where all participants joined together on stage, dancing to festive Teej songs and celebrating unity through joyful movement. The program was a wonderful blend of culture, entertainment, and fellowship that strengthened bonds across clubs and celebrated the spirit of Teej.",
    objectives: "To celebrate the cultural festival of Teej with joy and togetherness among Rotaract members.To promote fellowship and strengthen bonds among multiple Rotaract clubs through collaborative celebration.To provide a platform for Rotaractors to showcase their talents through dance, music, poetry, and games.To create a lively and inclusive environment that encourages interaction, entertainment, and cultural appreciation.To highlight the importance of preserving and celebrating Nepali traditions within the youth community",
