    excerpt: "Club COTS empowered members with the knowledge and skills needed for effective leadership, enhanced coordination, and strengthened the foundation for impactful service and smooth club…",
    body: "The Club Officers Training Seminar (COTS) was successfully conducted under the guidance of Assistant District Leadership Trainer (ADLT) Rtr. Arjun Khadka. The primary objective of the session was to equip the newly appointed board members with the essential knowledge and leadership skills required for effective club management. COTS helps Rotaract members learn about club management, leadership development, community service, and Rotaract’s values, making it a vital preparatory session for the incoming term. The session included detailed training on the responsibilities of various club roles, strategies for efficient administration, project planning, financial transparency, and strengthening Rotary-Rotaract relations. The training was held immediately after a regular club meeting at 11:00 AM, and prior to the start, the checklist for club COTS logistics was reviewed. This included materials such as A4-sized paper, chart papers, pens, and tokens of love. A financial discussion was also conducted to settle the expenses incurred during the program, which totaled Rs. 680. The cost was shared equally between the two clubs, with each contributing Rs. 340. The session concluded with an open floor for queries, followed by feedback and a group photo. Overall, COTS proved to be an insightful and productive initiative to build a strong and well-informed leadership team for the club's upcoming term.",
    objectives: "To educate club officers and members about effective club management practices.To develop leadership skills necessary for leading successful Rotaract projects and teams.To enhance understanding of community service planning and execution.To reinforce the core values and principles of Rotaract.To build confidence in handling club responsibilities and improve team coordination.To prepare the club for a well-structured and impactful Rotaract year ahead.",
