    body: "On 24th August 2024, a joint meeting between the Rotaract Club of Metro City and the Rotaract Club of Jawalakhel Manjushree was held at Molish School, Lagankhel, Lalitpur, from 10:30 AM to 11:02 AM. This marked the 362nd regular meeting of RAC Metro City and the 321st of RAC Jawalakhel Manjushree. The meeting was chaired by Rtr. Sweta Shrestha, President of RAC Metro City, and Rtr. Shraddha Shakya, President of RAC Jawalakhel Manjushree. The primary objective of the meeting was the exchange of letterheads, symbolizing fellowship, partnership, and mutual commitment to future collaboration. In addition to this, key agendas discussed included feedback on the recently conducted Matya Health Camp and deliberation on the Club Cots initiative as a potential joint project. An open floor session also provided space for members to share ideas, feedback, and explore further avenues of collaboration. The meeting concluded successfully, strengthening the bond between the two clubs and laying the groundwork for continued cooperation.",
    objectives: "To formally conduct a joint meeting fostering fellowship and understanding between both clubs.To exchange official letterheads, symbolizing mutual respect, partnership, and a commitment to future collaboration.To provide a platform for reviewing recent joint initiatives like the Matya Health Camp and gathering feedback.To deliberate on potential collaborative projects, such as the Club COTS, ensuring better coordination and planning.To create an open space for members from both clubs to exchange ideas, share experiences, and explore opportunities for synergy.To strengthen inter-club relationships, promote teamwork, and uphold the spirit of Rotaract unity.",
