    cover: "https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1747742416-b88950c2-3ab7-4a72-988a-21cc7224a47d.jpeg",
    gallery: ["https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1747742416-b88950c2-3ab7-4a72-988a-21cc7224a47d.jpeg", "https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1747742416-f8ea48dd-d591-4fe6-893a-b28f58bc57eb.jpeg", "https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1747742416-260a0ed3-c346-4490-8e8e-3619a63152a3.jpeg", "https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1747742416-d4ec408c-2b96-4b2f-9533-3d70503e70a5.jpeg", "https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1747742416-d89adf27-46da-416b-9341-bc51230f6456.jpeg", "https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1747742416-3b4f35f6-f113-4bde-bbfc-ae62a8679a47.jpeg"],
    excerpt: "The Matya Health Camp 2024 benefited over 500 devotees by ensuring their well-being during the strenuous festival, while also strengthening the fellowship among Rotaract Clubs of Zone…",
    body: "On August 21, 2024, the Rotaract Clubs of Zone XII, including the Rotaract Club of Metro City, collaboratively organized the Mataya Health Camp 2024 during the culturally significant Mataya festival held in Patan. This Buddhist festival, observed in memory of departed loved ones, involves devotees walking barefoot for long distances through the streets of Patan, making health support a vital component of the celebration.\n\nThe camp was conducted from 7:00 AM to 7:00 PM, with service stalls set up at Bhinsebahal, Ta:bahal, and Shrebahal. Over 500 devotees were served through the provision of glucose water, basic first aid, foot massages, and refreshments. The initiative offered relief to physically exhausted participants and contributed to their safety and comfort during the rigorous pilgrimage.\n\nThe health camp was a testament to zonal fellowship, with seven clubs coming together to support a shared mission. Volunteers gained valuable experience in teamwork, leadership, and event coordination, while also demonstrating compassion and commitment to public welfare. The participation of Interactors added to the collaborative spirit, and all service points were thoroughly cleaned at the end of the day.\n\nThe Mataya Health Camp 2024 effectively combined cultural preservation, community service, and Rotaract values, leaving a lasting impact on both the participants and the general public. The initiative reflected the strength of collaboration among Zone XII clubs and reinforced Rotaract’s presence in meaningful public health and cultural engagements.",
    objectives: "To support devotees participating in the Mataya festival by providing hydration, first aid, and physical relief.To promote public health and safety during a strenuous cultural event.To foster collaboration and fellowship among the Rotaract Clubs of Zone XII.To preserve and honor cultural traditions through meaningful community service.To provide Rotaractors with practical experience in volunteerism, teamwork, and event management.To enhance the visibility and positive impact of Rotaract in local communities through active engagement.",
