    excerpt: "The physiotherapy training empowered Rotaractors with practical skills to serve their communities more effectively during health camps and cultural events, enhancing both their…",
    body: "A two-day Physiotherapy Training Session was successfully conducted on the 19th and 20th of August, 2024, at Blue Lotus Hospital, Satdobato, Lalitpur, jointly organized by the Rotaract Clubs of Zone XII. This training was specifically designed for enthusiastic Rotaractors who were willing to provide physiotherapy services to individuals in need during community outreach programs, health camps, and cultural events.\n\nThe session was led by professional physiotherapists who trained participants on basic therapeutic techniques, muscle relaxation, and physical rehabilitation methods. The training played a crucial role in preparing the Rotaractors to assist during the Matya Health Camp, held as part of the traditional Matya Festival in Patan. This festival involves extensive barefoot walking by devotees, often resulting in muscle fatigue and discomfort. Through this training, Rotaractors were empowered to offer practical support to alleviate such physical strain, particularly among elderly and vulnerable individuals.\n\nThe collaboration among the clubs of Zone XII showcased unity in purpose and strengthened inter-club bonds while enhancing the service capabilities of the participating members. The training was highly beneficial in building a team of capable volunteers ready to serve with both compassion and competence.",
    objectives: "• To equip Rotaractors with basic physiotherapy skills to support individuals during community outreach and health camps.\n\n• To prepare members to provide effective relief and care during cultural events like the Matya Festival, where physical strain is common.\n\n• To enhance the capacity of Rotaractors in health-related service delivery through professional guidance.\n\n• To promote collaboration and knowledge sharing among the Rotaract Clubs of Zone XII.\n\n• To build a network of trained volunteers ready to assist during medical emergencies or special service occasions.",
