    excerpt: "The tree plantation program enhanced environmental sustainability while strengthening community ties. It also fostered collaboration between the Rotaract Club, Rotary Club, local…",
    body: "The Tree Plantation Program was successfully conducted in Dakshinkali Municipality, Ward No. 01, Kathmandu, in collaboration with the Rotary Club of Kathmandu Metro. As part of the club’s ongoing commitment to environmental sustainability and community service, a total of 200 saplings were planted in a dedicated effort to restore greenery and promote ecological balance in the area. The program saw the active participation of Rotaractors, Rotarians, local residents, and community leaders, making it a collective effort toward a greener future.\n\nA notable aspect of the event was the strong support extended by the Local Police of Chalnakhel, who not only ensured the safety and coordination of the program but also took part in the plantation activities, encouraging civic responsibility and environmental awareness. The local community members also played a vital role by assisting in identifying suitable plantation spots, preparing the site, and helping plant and water the saplings. Their enthusiastic involvement reflected a deep sense of ownership and responsibility towards preserving the natural environment of their locality.\n\nThe initiative aimed to combat deforestation, reduce the effects of climate change, and improve air quality while fostering a sense of unity and collaboration among stakeholders. The presence and participation of both the police and the local people added to the program’s credibility and impact, ensuring the sustainability of the effort by promising to care for the planted trees in the days to come. This successful event not only enhanced environmental consciousness but also strengthened the relationship between the Rotaract Club, Rotary Club, and the local community, setting a strong foundation for future collaborative service projects.",
    objectives: "To promote environmental sustainability and ecological balance.To increase green coverage in Dakshinkali Municipality, Ward No. 01.To combat deforestation and reduce the impact of climate change.To improve air quality and contribute to a healthier environment.To raise awareness about the importance of trees and conservation.To strengthen collaboration between the Rotaract Club and Rotary Club of Kathmandu Metro in service initiatives.",
