    excerpt: "Conducting an installation ceremony helps formally transition leadership and recognize incoming board members. It also strengthens club unity, renews commitment, and showcases the…",
    body: "The 12th Installation Ceremony of the Rotaract Club of Metro City was a significant and well-structured event held to officially transition the club's leadership and recognize the efforts of the outgoing board while welcoming the new team for the upcoming Rotaract year. The ceremony began with a formal announcement and welcome of dignitaries, including club leaders, district representatives, and special guests. National and Rotary anthems were followed by a symbolic inauguration through the lighting of the Panas. A warm welcome speech and cultural dance enriched the atmosphere.\n\nOutgoing President Rtr. Ashesha Mali presented a detailed annual report, highlighting key accomplishments, followed by distribution of certificates to board members and supporters. The incoming President Rtr. Sweta Shrestha was introduced, took her oath, and symbolically received the club’s insignia - charter certificate, collar, gong, and gavel - marking the leadership handover. She delivered an inspiring acceptance speech and introduced the new board, who also took their oaths and received official appointments, pins, and ID cards.\n\nThe event also included the induction of new members, speeches by dignitaries, recognition of the outgoing president, and distribution of tokens of appreciation to guests. The program concluded with a vote of thanks, formal toast proposals for national and international goodwill, and adjournment by the new president, followed by refreshments. The ceremony reflected the club’s dedication to continuity, growth, and community service.",
    objectives: "To officially induct new president, board of directors and members, marking the formal beginning of the new tenure (RY 2024-25).",
