    excerpt: "Panel discussion on exclusive breastfeeding offers participants valuable insights into its numerous advantages for both infants and mothers, including enhanced immunity and reduced…",
    body: "Rotaract Club of Metro City collaborated a Panel Discussion on Effective Breastfeeding on 7th August 2024 with the 21 different Rotaract clubs which was facilitated by President Rtr. Dipesh Tikhatri (RAC Baneshwor Royal) and panelist were Dr. Archana Nepal, RN. Ritu Ghimire and RN Rita Malik. Effective Breastfeeding aims to provide an infant with all the nutrients and hydration they need during the first six months of life and also supports optimal growth and development, strengthens the immune system, and fosters a close bond between mother and baby. This event helps participants gain valuable insights into best practices, practical tips, and the health benefits of breastfeeding and provides an opportunity to address common challenges, misconceptions, and concerns while fostering support networks among parents and experts.",
