    gallery: ["https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1747890578-adacf2ad-937b-48f8-9ead-def968815fb7.jpeg", "https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1747890578-414ffb9d-56a6-40e0-885e-1978b62610c6.jpeg"],
    excerpt: "The fellowship allowed members to connect on a deeper level beyond formal meetings, fostering a sense of unity and belonging. It encouraged personal sharing, professional learning, and…",
    body: "On 3rd August 2024, the Rotaract Club of Metro City organized an Internal Club Fellowship at the culturally rich location of Pimbahal, Patan, Lalitpur. The primary objective of the fellowship was to strengthen the bond among club members through informal discussions, shared experiences, and lighthearted activities. Members gathered in a relaxed setting and engaged in meaningful conversations on a wide range of topics, including their personal lives, professional growth, and the current political landscape of Nepal. These discussions created a space for openness, learning, and mutual understanding.\n\nAdding to the delight of the day, everyone enjoyed delicious food and took a peaceful walk around the iconic Pimbahal Pond, soaking in the heritage and calm surroundings. The fellowship was further enriched by the presence of two distinguished Rotaractors-Rtr. Peshal Bhattarai, Past President of RAC Patan, and Rtr. Girish Shakhya, Charter President of RAC Bhadrapur. Their presence added significant value as they shared inspiring stories from their Rotaract journeys, offering guidance and motivation to the members of RAC Metro City.\n\nThe event proved to be a wholesome and rejuvenating experience. It not only deepened interpersonal connections among members but also reinforced the spirit of unity and shared purpose within the club. The Rotaract Club of Metro City remains committed to organizing such fellowships that foster camaraderie, dialogue, and continuous personal as well as collective growth.",
    objectives: "To strengthen the bond and camaraderie among club membersTo provide a relaxed platform for open dialogue and experience sharingTo encourage conversations on personal growth and professional developmentTo promote awareness and discussion on current national political issuesTo offer an informal space for interaction with senior and experienced RotaractorsTo enhance the overall fellowship culture within the club",
