    gallery: ["https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1747754262-46f28b3b-b744-44be-8567-00b4c01ef380.jpg", "https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1747754262-2e2579b5-9b1f-450b-84dd-951d6ccc80a6.jpg", "https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1747754262-d13bcc0e-996d-4f84-8f71-fa97f5abdb93.jpg"],
    excerpt: "The Blood Donation Program provided a vital contribution to the local healthcare system by collecting 42 units of blood, potentially saving numerous lives. It also promoted community…",
    body: "On 27th July 2024, the Rotaract Club of Metro City, in collaboration with the Rotary Club of Kathmandu Metro, organized a successful Blood Donation Program at Buddha Park, Swayambhu, Kathmandu. The event began at 9:00 AM and concluded at 2:00 PM, drawing active participation from local residents, youth volunteers, and club members. A total of 42 units of blood were collected during the program, contributing meaningfully to local blood banks and emergency reserves.\n\nThe primary goal of the initiative was to promote voluntary blood donation and support the healthcare system by ensuring the availability of safe blood. The program was conducted under the supervision of trained medical personnel, with all necessary health and safety protocols in place to ensure the well-being of donors.\n\nThis collaborative effort reflected the shared commitment of both clubs to community service and public health. The event not only helped meet critical medical needs but also raised awareness about the importance of regular blood donation. Overall, the Blood Donation Program was a significant success, reinforcing the impact of teamwork and civic responsibility in serving society.",
    objectives: "To encourage voluntary blood donation among the community.To support local hospitals and blood banks by collecting adequate units of blood.To raise awareness about the importance and benefits of regular blood donation.To promote the values of social responsibility and humanitarian service among club members and the public.To strengthen collaboration between the Rotaract Club of Metro City and the Rotary Club of Kathmandu Metro through a meaningful community initiative.",
