    id: "50721",
    title: "Grant Management Seminar",
    slug: "grant-management-seminar-50721",
    avenue: "The Rotary Foundation",
    projectType: "Participated",
    tenure: "2024-25",
    status: "Completed",
    date: "2024-06-22",
    endDate: "2025-05-23",
    location: "Microsoft Teams",
    category: "Training / Workshops",
    cover: "https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1748003664-e6d6a0d5-7838-4572-a56b-4f56f65e49a3.png",
    gallery: ["https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1748003664-e6d6a0d5-7838-4572-a56b-4f56f65e49a3.png", "https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1748003664-67a183ac-4d4b-4eb8-9f29-68dab3bc38f9.png", "https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1748003664-f05cb1da-01f5-479a-9ab3-9a42b4cbb3ba.png"],
    excerpt: "This training helped us confidently navigate the Rotary Global Grant process, meet eligibility requirements, and design impactful projects aligned with Rotary’s goals.",
    body: "The District Grant Management Seminar, organized by Rotaract District 3292, was held online via Microsoft Teams on 22nd June 2024 and was attended by over 200 Rotaractors from across the district. The primary aim of the seminar was to educate and equip Rotaractors with the knowledge and practical skills necessary to design, apply for, and manage Rotary grants effectively. The event commenced with opening remarks by District Governor Rtn. Rajendra Prasad Dhoju, followed by the presence of key dignitaries including District Governor Elect Rtn. Rajendra Man Shrechan, District Leadership Facilitator PDG Jitendra Rajbhandari, District Rotaract Representative Rtr. Roshan Karki, and District Rotaract Representative Elect Rtr. Bikram Chhetri.\n\nThe seminar was divided into two key sessions. The first session, titled “Designing a Project,” was led by Mr. Rajendra Lamsal, District International Service Chair and CADRE Member of The Rotary Foundation (2020-2028). He explained various types of Rotary grants such as Global Grants, District Grants, and Disaster Relief Grants, and highlighted the critical components of successful grant proposals, including community need assessment, sustainability, measurable outcomes, SMART goals, detailed budgeting, and strategic partnerships. He emphasized the importance of using resources like the Grant Center on the My Rotary website to strengthen proposals.\n\nThe second session, “How to Apply for Grants?”, was conducted by Mr. Sudip Koirala, who guided participants through the full grant application process. He outlined preparatory steps such as conducting a Needs Assessment, drafting a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU), and establishing a well-developed project and budget plan. He elaborated on how Global Grants are financed, with club contributions matched by The Rotary Foundation, and gave a step-by-step walkthrough of the grant application process. Mr. Koirala also emphasized the importance of financial management, report writing, documentation, and transparency throughout project implementation.\n\nThe seminar concluded with an interactive Q&A session, where attendees clarified their queries related to both project design and grant application processes. This comprehensive training provided participants with the essential tools and understanding to engage in impactful service initiatives backed by Rotary grants.",
    objectives: "To learn how the Rotary Foundation’s grant process works, step by step.To understand who can apply for Global Grants and what’s needed to qualify.To find out how to create clear, meaningful projects that match Rotary’s main goals.",
