    excerpt: "Encourages members to uphold high standards of service and leadership, strengthening club unity and dedication",
    body: "The Rotaract Club of Metro City recently organized a successful District Rotaract Representative (DRR) visit at German Homes, attended by DRR Rtr. Roshan Karki, Assistant District Rotaract Representative (ADRR) Rtr. Chandra Bhakta Aacharya, and Zone Rotaract Representative (ZRR) Rtr. Dinesh Ghimire.\n\nADRR Rtr. Chandra Bhakta Aacharya began the visit by thoroughly reviewing our club's documents, highlighting both the correct aspects and areas needing improvement. His constructive feedback was invaluable for ensuring our records meet Rotaract standards.\n\nWe then moved on to the presentation segment, where each avenue director showcased the projects and initiatives undertaken by our club throughout the year. These presentations demonstrated our commitment to service and community development, covering a wide range of activities and achievements.\n\nDRR Rtr. Roshan Karki, ADRR Rtr. Chandra Bhakta Aacharya, and ZRR Rtr. Dinesh Ghimire provided insightful feedback and suggestions, which were highly appreciated. Their guidance will help us refine our processes and enhance our future projects.\n\nThe visit concluded on a celebratory note with a cake-cutting ceremony. We also presented tokens of love to our esteemed guests as a gesture of gratitude for their time and contributions. This visit has strengthened our club’s operations and motivated us to continue our journey of service and community development.",
    objectives: "- Ensure club documents meet Rotaract standards.\n\n- Showcase achievements from the past year.\n\n- Receive valuable feedback from DRR, ADRR, and ZRR.\n\n- Foster motivation for continued service and excellence.\n\n- Express gratitude to the visiting representatives with a celebratory ceremony.",
