    cover: "https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1715340093-cd9b32f4-feee-4439-b1e8-aef883e73844.jpg",
    gallery: ["https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1715340093-cd9b32f4-feee-4439-b1e8-aef883e73844.jpg", "https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1715340093-de1a49a5-c110-4ee8-afec-46ef2593a4bf.jpg", "https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1715340093-dd2a55a8-0b5b-41a3-94c2-6214d0daeb14.jpg", "https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1715340093-4b31b228-3331-45e3-9721-e96e7a90c2ea.jpg", "https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1715340093-9def8af1-ec2c-4469-a766-66bbafcf6caf.jpeg"],
    excerpt: "N/A",
    body: "The Rotaract Club of Metro City recently extended a helping hand to the Balaju Old Age Home by donating essential cleaning kits. These kits comprised crucial items such as hand wash, bucket mop, floor cleaner, toilet cleaner, and more. This act of generosity was a concerted effort by our club, aimed at improving the living conditions of the elderly residents at the facility.\n\nDuring our visit, we had the opportunity to engage with some of the senior citizens and learn about the challenges they face on a daily basis. Among them, we encountered individuals who were coping with mental disabilities. Witnessing their joy and gratitude upon receiving these materials was truly heartening. The Balaju Old Age Home accommodates a total of 47 residents, all of whom greatly appreciated the support extended by our club. By providing them with these essential cleaning supplies, we hope to contribute to a cleaner and more comfortable living environment for the elderly members of our community.",
    objectives: "Rotaract Club of Metro City donated cleaning kits to Balaju Old Age Home.Kits included hand wash, bucket mop, floor cleaner, toilet cleaner, etc.Interaction with residents revealed some facing mental disabilities.Mentally disabled residents were delighted with the supplies.Total of 47 members reside in the old age home.Donation aimed to improve living conditions and was greatly appreciated.",
