    cover: "https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1692465375-361948361_820594909356171_3019921615733129221_n.jpg",
    gallery: ["https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1692465375-361948361_820594909356171_3019921615733129221_n.jpg", "https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1692465375-362033352_3427411500859315_3018759905372106395_n.jpg", "https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1692465375-362183461_314438427677264_2733100904734735380_n.jpg", "https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1692465375-362284891_626278939602894_2126985682840336909_n.jpg", "https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1692465375-362293616_166217706473347_2678151403757839529_n.jpg", "https://my.rotaract3292.org/storage/report_images/1692465375-362301057_1690347901426540_4965051619447666429_n.jpg"],
    excerpt: "N/A",
    body: "On July 22nd, the Rotaract Club of Metro City proudly held its 11th Installation Ceremony at National College, Dhumabarahi. The event was graced by the presence of over 60 enthusiastic participants, making it a remarkable occasion.\n\nThe ceremony was honored by the esteemed presence of the President of our parent club, the Rotary Club of Kathmandu Metro, Rtn. C Mani Chaulagain, and the Secretary, Rtn. Ramesh Neupane, who served as the chief guests. Additionally, our District Rotaract Representative (DRR), Rtr. Roshan Karki, and Assistant District Rotaract Representative (ADRR), Rtr. Lok Raj Pandey, attended as district guests, lending their support and encouragement.\n\nOur past presidents were also in attendance, offering their invaluable guidance and unwavering support throughout the event. Their presence underscored the continuity and strength of our club's leadership.\n\nA highlight of the ceremony was the induction of five new general members into the Rotaract Club of Metro City. This significant addition reflects our ongoing growth and commitment to community service and leadership development.\n\nThe Installation Ceremony not only marked the beginning of a new term but also celebrated the spirit of camaraderie and dedication within our Rotaract community. We look forward to an exciting year ahead, filled with meaningful projects and initiatives.",
    objectives: "- Ensure active participation with over 60 attendees present, fostering a sense of community and commitment among members.\n\n- Host distinguished guests including the President and Secretary of the Rotary Club of Kathmandu Metro, enhancing club prestige and collaboration.\n\n- Welcome District Rotaract Representative (DRR) and Assistant District Rotaract Representative (ADRR), promoting regional cooperation and support.\n\n- Seek guidance and support from past presidents, ensuring continuity and leadership development within the club.\n\n- Induct five new general members, expanding club membership and strengthening the team for future endeavors.\n\n- Celebrate the accomplishments of past terms while inspiring future success and community impact.",
